# 🤖 Cursor Rules & Constraints

## 🎯 Component Strategy

### shadcn/ui First Policy
```typescript
// ✅ Use shadcn components as foundation
import { Button } from '@/components/ui/button';
import { Card, CardContent, CardHeader } from '@/components/ui/card';

// ❌ Don't create custom buttons/cards from scratch
const CustomButton = () => <div className="...">; // Avoid
```

### Component Creation Rules
1. **Check shadcn first**: Always verify if component exists
2. **Extend, don't replace**: Use `className` prop to customize  
3. **Compose over configure**: Combine simple components vs complex variants
4. **Export patterns**: Use default exports for pages, named for utilities

### When to Create Custom Components
- **Layout primitives**: Container, Section (already created)
- **Business logic**: ServiceCard, BookingFlow (domain-specific)
- **Compositions**: Hero sections, feature blocks
- **Never create**: Basic buttons, inputs, cards, modals

## 🎨 Styling Constraints

### No Hard-Coded Values
```typescript
// ✅ Use design tokens
className="bg-brand-text text-brand-bg p-6 rounded-xl"
className="text-gold hover:text-gold/90"

// ❌ Never hard-code
className="bg-[#1C1A1A] text-[#FAF8F7]" // Forbidden
style={{ color: '#CFB27C' }} // Forbidden
```

### Color Usage Rules
- **Brand colors only**: `brand-text`, `brand-bg`, `brand-accent`
- **System colors**: `blush`, `mauve`, `gold`, `ink`, `porcelain`
- **shadcn colors**: `background`, `foreground`, `muted`, etc.
- **Forbidden**: Any hex codes, RGB values, blue gradients

### Spacing System
```typescript
// ✅ Follow 8px rhythm
className="p-6 mb-8 gap-4" // 24px, 32px, 16px
className="py-12 md:py-16" // Section spacing

// ❌ Random spacing
className="p-7 mb-13" // Breaks rhythm
className="ml-[23px]" // Arbitrary values forbidden
```

## 🌐 Internationalization Rules

### Always Use Translations
```typescript
// ✅ Proper i18n usage
import { useTranslations } from 'next-intl';

const Component = () => {
  const t = useTranslations('nav');
  return <button>{t('booking')}</button>;
};

// ❌ Hard-coded strings forbidden
return <button>Book Now</button>; // Never
return <p>Rezervēt tagad</p>; // Never, even in Latvian
```

### Translation Key Strategy
- Use `useTranslations('domain')` for scoped keys
- Prefer hierarchical keys: `hero.title`, `form.submit`
- Include context in ambiguous keys: `button.save.booking`
- Test all languages during development

## 🏗️ Architecture Patterns

### File Organization
```
src/
├── app/[locale]/           # Next.js app router pages
├── components/             # Reusable components
│   ├── ui/                # shadcn components (don't modify)
│   ├── Header.tsx         # Layout components
│   └── ServiceCard.tsx    # Business components
├── data/                  # Static data, types
├── lib/                   # Utilities, helpers
└── styles/                # Design tokens, globals
```

### Import Preferences
```typescript
// ✅ Absolute imports with @/ alias
import Container from '@/components/Container';
import { serviceCategories } from '@/data/services';

// ❌ Relative imports for cross-directory
import Container from '../../components/Container'; // Avoid
```

### Component Structure
```typescript
// ✅ Preferred component pattern
'use client'; // Only when needed

import { ComponentProps } from 'react';
import { useTranslations } from 'next-intl';

interface ComponentNameProps {
  required: string;
  optional?: boolean;
  className?: string;
}

export default function ComponentName({
  required,
  optional = false,
  className
}: ComponentNameProps) {
  const t = useTranslations('domain');
  
  return (
    <div className={cn("base-styles", className)}>
      {/* Implementation */}
    </div>
  );
}
```

## 🚫 Forbidden Patterns

### Styling Anti-Patterns
```typescript
// ❌ Inline styles
<div style={{ marginTop: '20px' }} />

// ❌ Blue colors (brand conflict)
className="bg-blue-500 text-blue-100"

// ❌ Hard-coded hex values  
className="border-[#FF0000]"

// ❌ Arbitrary spacing
className="ml-[23px] pt-[7px]"

// ❌ Non-semantic HTML
<div onClick={handleClick}>Click me</div> // Use <button>
```

### Code Anti-Patterns
```typescript
// ❌ Overly complex variant systems
const buttonVariants = cva("base", {
  variants: {
    size: { xs: "", sm: "", md: "", lg: "", xl: "", 2xl: "" },
    color: { /* 10+ colors */ },
    style: { /* 5+ styles */ }
  }
}); // Too complex, compose instead

// ❌ Non-semantic component names
const Wrapper = () => {}; // Use Container, Section, etc.
const Thing = () => {};   // Be descriptive

// ❌ Prop drilling beyond 2-3 levels
<ComponentA config={config}>
  <ComponentB config={config}>
    <ComponentC config={config} /> // Use context or state management
  </ComponentB>
</ComponentA>
```

## ✅ Preferred Patterns

### Composition Over Configuration
```typescript
// ✅ Compose simple components
<Card className="border-gold/30">
  <CardHeader>
    <CardTitle className="font-serif">Title</CardTitle>
  </CardHeader>
  <CardContent>Content</CardContent>
</Card>

// ❌ Complex variant systems
<Card variant="featured" theme="gold" size="large" />
```

### Semantic HTML Structure
```typescript
// ✅ Semantic elements
<main>
  <Section as="section" spacing="xl">
    <Container>
      <article>
        <header>
          <h1>Page Title</h1>
        </header>
        <p>Content</p>
      </article>
    </Container>
  </Section>
</main>

// ❌ Div soup
<div>
  <div>
    <div>
      <div>Content</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
```

### State Management
```typescript
// ✅ URL state for user-facing data
const [service, setService] = useState(searchParams.get('service'));

// ✅ Local state for UI interactions
const [isMenuOpen, setIsMenuOpen] = useState(false);

// ✅ Context for cross-component data
const { user, booking } = useBookingContext();

// ❌ Global state for everything
const globalState = useGlobalStore(); // Avoid unless necessary
```

## 🎭 Animation Guidelines

### Motion Constraints
```typescript
// ✅ Consistent timing
const fadeInUp = {
  initial: { opacity: 0, y: 20 },
  animate: { opacity: 1, y: 0 },
  transition: { duration: 0.24, ease: "easeOut" }
};

// ✅ Stagger timing
staggerChildren: 0.06 // 60ms delay

// ❌ Random timing
transition: { duration: 0.37, ease: "easeInOut" } // Be consistent
```

### Animation Rules
- Use 240ms for content entrance
- Use 60ms for stagger delays  
- Use 200ms for hover effects
- Always respect `prefers-reduced-motion`
- Avoid decorative animations

## 📱 Responsive Design

### Mobile-First Approach
```typescript
// ✅ Mobile-first responsive classes
className="text-base md:text-lg lg:text-xl"
className="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3"

// ❌ Desktop-first (harder to maintain)
className="text-xl lg:text-lg md:text-base" // Confusing cascade
```

### Breakpoint Usage
- **Default**: Mobile (0-768px)
- **md**: Tablet (768px+)  
- **lg**: Desktop (1024px+)
- **xl**: Large desktop (1280px+)
- **2xl**: Extra large (1536px+)

## 🔧 Performance Rules

### Component Optimization
```typescript
// ✅ Lazy load heavy components
const BookingWidget = dynamic(() => import('./BookingWidget'), {
  loading: () => <Skeleton className="h-96" />
});

// ✅ Memoize expensive calculations
const expensiveValue = useMemo(() => heavyComputation(data), [data]);

// ❌ Inline object/function creation in render
<Component style={{ margin: 10 }} onClick={() => handleClick()} />
```

### Image Optimization
```typescript
// ✅ Always use Next.js Image
import Image from 'next/image';

<Image
  src="/hero.jpg"
  alt="Descriptive alt text"
  width={1200}
  height={800}
  priority={isAboveFold}
/>

// ❌ Regular img tags
<img src="/hero.jpg" /> // Forbidden in production
```

